<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Southern Song</h1><p class="st-meta">1127 CE – 1279 CE · capital Lin'an (Hangzhou)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Song dynasty's southern phase, ruled from Hangzhou, when China led the world in commerce, technology and learning before falling to the Mongols.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234">Jin dynasty</a> (1115-1234) captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> in 1127, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-song">Zhao Gou</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong">Emperor Huizong</a>, was enthroned as Emperor Gaozong. Pursued south, he eventually fixed his court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Lin'an</a> (Hangzhou). The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shaoxing">Treaty of Shaoxing</a> in 1141 recognised the Huai river as the frontier, and the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yue-fei">Yue Fei</a>, who had opposed peace, was executed soon after.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Cut off from the north, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> flourished in the south. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> agriculture, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> expanded; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> circulated widely; and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanzhou">Quanzhou</a> became one of the world's great ports. A permanent navy guarded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> and coast. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhu-xi">Zhu Xi's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-confucianism">Neo-Confucianism</a> became orthodoxy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> was perhaps the world's largest city.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> to destroy Jin in 1234, then faced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> alone. After the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-xiangyang">siege of Xiangyang</a> ended in 1273, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Lin'an</a> surrendered in 1276. At the naval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yamen">Battle of Yamen</a> in 1279 the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-xiufu">Lu Xiufu</a> leapt into the sea with the boy emperor, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> ruled all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/southern-song.jpg" alt="Southern Song" width="320" height="315"><figcaption>Image: China - Song Dynasty - cs.svg: User:Mozzan derivative work: Kanguole · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China_-_Song_Dynasty-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1127 CE – 1279 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lin'an (Hangzhou)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zhao Gou (Emperor Gaozong), Zhao Shen (Emperor Xiaozong), Zhao Bing</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Neo-Confucianism, Buddhism, Daoism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Southern Song dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1203&amp;focus=southern-song" aria-label="Southern Song on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7581 918 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Southern Song lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10